F9A0 BDEA1E           (        forth.asm):04124 (7)             jsr     MIN2PST         2 parameters need to be stacked up
                      (        forth.asm):04125         * Register allocation notes:
                      (        forth.asm):04126         * X: pointer to ud1 (ARG_U/p in the C code).
                      (        forth.asm):04127         * Y: pointer to ud2 (ARG_V/q in the C code).
                      (        forth.asm):04128         * E: Inner loop index (i in the C code).
                      (        forth.asm):04129         * F: Outer loop index (j in the C code).
                      (        forth.asm):04130         *
                      (        forth.asm):04131         * We save U to the system stack and use it to point to a scratch area allocated
                      (        forth.asm):04132         * from the system stack that will contain the 4 bytes (double cell) ultimately
                      (        forth.asm):04133         * holding the result (MSB first, what else?).
                      (        forth.asm):04134         *
                      (        forth.asm):04135         * System stack structure:
                      (        forth.asm):04136         * ,S    Result scratch area (Result MSB)
                      (        forth.asm):04137         * 2,S   Result scratch area (Result LSB)
                      (        forth.asm):04138         * 4,S   Saved U register
